&lt;p&gt;Hudson River Trading (HRT) is seeking a Senior Immigration Specialist to manage our UK sponsor licence and oversee the end-to-end immigration lifecycle for sponsored workers. In this role, you will manage visa applications and compliance requirements, advise recruiters, managers, and employees on complex immigration matters, and support related needs across our UK and Ireland offices.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt;Serve as a Level 1 User on the Home Office Sponsorship Management System (SMS)&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Prepare and assign Certificates of Sponsorship (CoS) and prepare Skilled Worker and dependant visa applications through the UKVI portal&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Submit CoS allocation requests and support sponsor licence and allocation renewals&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Advise recruiters, managers, and employees on immigration options, case procedures, and processing timelines&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Support business visa applications for our UK and Ireland offices, including invitation letters and supporting documentation&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate immigration case records, databases, and internal visa reports&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Track work authorisation expiry dates and filing deadlines&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Review eligibility documents and assess potential immigration options and benefits&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Support immigration compliance, research, and ad hoc projects across the UK and Ireland&lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt; &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;At least 10 years of UK immigration experience, including case management responsibilities&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Experience with the Skilled Worker and Government Authorised Exchange (GAE) routes, Appendix D, Appendix Skilled Occupations, and UKVI compliance&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Experience developing visa strategies, assessing job categories, preparing defined CoS applications, and assigning CoS&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;In-depth knowledge of procedural and filing requirements across UK visa processes&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Experience using the Home Office SMS and UKVI websites&lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-value=&quot;{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:2,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Hudson River Trading (HRT) brings a scientific approach to trading financial products. We have built one of the world&#39;s most sophisticated computing environments for research and development. Our researchers are at the forefront of innovation in the world of algorithmic trading. 

At HRT we come from a variety of disciplines: mathematics and computer science, physics, and engineering, media and tech. We’re a community of self-starters who are motivated by the excitement of being at the cutting edge of automation in every part of our organization - from trading, to business operations, to recruiting and beyond. Our culture celebrates great ideas whether they come from HRT veterans or new hires. At HRT we’re friends and colleagues – whether we are sharing a meal, playing the latest board game, or writing elegant code. We embrace a culture of togetherness that extends far beyond the walls of our office.

Feel like you belong at HRT? Our goal is to find the best people and bring them together to do great work in a place where everyone is valued. HRT is proud of our diverse staff; we have offices all over the globe and benefit from our varied and unique perspectives. HRT is an equal opportunity employer; so whoever you are we’d love to get to know you.&amp;quot;}&quot; data-sheets-userformat=&quot;{&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:13185,&amp;quot;3&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:0},&amp;quot;10&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;11&amp;quot;:4,&amp;quot;12&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;15&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;IBM Plex Sans&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;16&amp;
